# 🔐 SOC Analyst Connection

Linux commands are frequently used during security investigations.

Example:

```text
Security Alert
      ↓
Identify affected Linux system
      ↓
Navigate filesystem
      ↓
Find relevant logs
      ↓
find
      ↓
Read logs
      ↓
cat / less / tail
      ↓
Search indicators
      ↓
grep
      ↓
Count events
      ↓
wc
      ↓
Investigate suspicious activity
```

### Example investigation

Suppose a SIEM alert reports:

```text
Multiple failed SSH login attempts
```

An analyst could investigate relevant authentication logs and search for:

```bash
grep "Failed" /var/log/auth.log
```

Then search for a specific source IP:

```bash
grep "192.168.1.50" /var/log/auth.log
```

The exact log path can vary by Linux distribution and logging configuration.

